# Target C: uniform polynomial-onset maximum-population wall classification

Date: 2026-10-07. Authority: audit.77.
**Proved candidate awaiting independent audit.** No canonical promotion.
Dependencies include the independently rederived proof-only effective chart,
fixed-wall first polytope and explicit one-deficit window from this run.

## 1. Statement and quantified advance

There is a universal constant c_*>0 such that for every integer M>=4 and
`0<theta<=c_* M^-40`, a unit-separated N=3M^2-3M+1-point cloud inside
the arithmetic six-sided sorting unit wall, clear of all wall vertices,
is exactly one of the finite sorting packets. In particular its center
and adjacent first-ring sites are an actual unit triangle. No smoothness
of the arbitrary cloud is required.

Combining the uniform one-deficit packet and finite Oler cap, the entire
wall class in this **joint growing-M interval** is excluded from a canonical
triangle-free source, with all exterior points and isolates retained.
The universal c_* is obtained by taking the minimum of finitely many
universal constants in the estimates below. No explicit numerical value
or sharp exponent is asserted. The exponent 40 is deliberately generous.
This is stronger than a separate unspecified onset for every fixed M.

`uniform chart -> polynomial active-row inverse and positive pinned stress
-> uniform isolation -> approximate rate/fiber classification -> exact
finite triangle for every M in the joint interval`.

This does not cover theta comparable to M^-3 or M^-1, arbitrary walls,
matching first profiles with different higher coefficients, or extraction
from an arbitrary canonical macroscopic container. It does not close C-II
or Level I. All constants C below are universal, independent of M and
of the M! rate permutations; enlarging C between estimates is allowed.

## 2. Flat active-row reconstruction from threshold paths

Fix a permutation pi of the arithmetic rates
`a_h=M-1-2h`, h=0,...,M-1. Let J be every moving-involving unit row in
its finite sorting packet, evaluated at theta=0. Strong rows S are all
ring edges and all six radial axes, including corner guards. A weak
row entering layer r at (r,j) is the unique unit incoming choice: A if
the new rate is not among the j smallest prefix rates, B otherwise.
Axis choices are strong; all off-axis choices are weak.

For any displacement x with full wall pinned, put
`eta=||R_0[J] x||_infinity`, and let ||x||_max be its largest vertex
Euclidean norm. We claim

`||x||_max <= 500 M^3 eta`.                                 (7)

Here is an explicit reconstruction, not a generic rank argument.
Radial telescoping from the pinned corners gives
`|e_k dot x(r e_k)|<=M eta`; the center norm is at most 2M eta.
Write each axial x as n_(r,k)e_k+alpha_(r,k)J(e_k).
Summing the r ring rows on a side and using |n|<=M eta gives
`|alpha_(r,k+1)-alpha_(r,k)|<=4M eta`.
Choose alpha_r=alpha_(r,0); all axial vectors differ from
alpha_r J(e_k) by at most 21M eta.

At an off-axis sector point define s from its u projection divided by
c=sqrt(3)/2, and replace its v projection by c(s+alpha_r). Ring
sums bound the change by 26M eta. Use the exact axial s=0,-alpha_r,
center zero and pinned wall zero. This defines a linear projection P_L
onto the strong-row kernel L, with

`||x-P_L x||_max<=26M eta`.                                 (8)

For d=P_L x, each active weak recurrence row has absolute residual at
most 62M eta after division by c. Let I_j be the positions of the j
smallest full permuted rates. The threshold path whose prefix selections
are I_j intersect {0,...,r-1} uses only J rows. Telescoping from center
to pinned boundary yields

`|sum_(h in I_j) t_h|<=62M^2 eta`,
`t_h=alpha_(h+1)-alpha_h`.

Adjacent j differences recover each t_h with error at most 124M^2 eta.
Thus |alpha_r|<=124M^3 eta. Every interior (r,j) lies on some full
threshold path; telescoping to it gives |s_(r,j)|<=186M^3 eta.
In Cartesian sector coordinates d=(c*s,s/2+alpha_r), so
||d||_max<=400M^3 eta. Together with (8), this proves (7).
It also gives

`smallest singular value of R_0[J] >= 1/(1000 M^4)`.

Applying (8) using only strong residuals gives a separate nonzero singular
bound `sigma_min^+(R_0[S])>=1/(52M^2)`: distance to L is at most the
Euclidean norm of x-P_Lx. These statements hold for every permutation.
The exact verifier independently checks active-path coverage and telescoped
linear identities; it does not infer a rank bound from floating singular
values.

## 3. Explicit positive normal weights, with polynomial bounds

Let d* be the first sorting field and lambda^p the central six-chain
stress. Its energy gradient is
`g_0=2 R_1^T lambda^p`.
On L, `g_0 dot x=12 sum_h a_(pi(h))*delta t_h`.
For increasing rates b_j, Abel summation gives

`sum b_j delta t_(position j)`
`=-sum_(j=1)^(M-1) (b_j-b_(j-1))*sum_(h in I_j) delta t_h`.

The threshold path row sum in any one sector is c times that subset
sum. Average the six sector paths. This represents g_0 on L as
`-R_0^T mu`, with

`mu_e=(2/c)*sum_(threshold paths containing e) (b_j-b_(j-1))`.

Every active weak row lies on at least one threshold path; hence mu_e>=4/c
there, and mu_e<=C M. The remaining force g_0+R_0^Tmu belongs to the
strong-row span. By the strong singular bound it has strong coefficients
nu with ||nu||_2<=C M^4. Therefore
`lambda_1=(mu-nu)/2` solves

`R_0^T lambda_1=-R_1^T lambda^p`,

with every weak coefficient at least 2/c and ||lambda_1||_2<=C M^4.
The unit-contact directions are single rate factors, so
`||R_1||<=C M`, `||R_2(theta)||<=C M^2`.

Add epsilon times the sum of the other nested stresses to lambda^p,
where `epsilon=c_0 M^-7` and c_0 is a sufficiently small universal
constant. The resulting lambda_0 is positive on every strong row,
with strong minimum epsilon and total sum at most C M. The extra first
force has norm at most C epsilon M^3; the J-row inverse bound permits
its correction with norm at most C epsilon M^7. Choose c_0 so the weak
lambda_1 coefficients stay at least one. The total first correction
still has norm at most C M^4. This uses nested stresses to construct
positive coefficients, not to add overlapping energy lower bounds.

For theta<=c M^-11, R_theta[J] has a right inverse of its transpose
of norm at most 2000M^4, by the preceding singular bound and
||R_theta-R_0||<=C M theta. The residual of
lambda_0+theta*lambda_1 is at most C theta^2 M^5. Correct it exactly
with that right inverse, by at most C theta^2 M^9. Shrink the universal
c so the final exact pinned stress lambda_theta obeys

`R_theta^T lambda_theta=0`,
`min_e lambda_theta,e >= theta/2`,
`sum_e lambda_theta,e <= C M`.

Strong positivity follows from epsilon dominating theta C M^4; weak
positivity follows from theta dominating C theta^2 M^9. All dependences
are polynomial and uniform over the permutation.

## 4. Uniform finite isolation

The infinity version of (7) remains valid for R_theta with constant
1000M^3, by absorbing C M^4 theta*||x||_max. For a feasible displacement
x from the sorting packet with the same pinned wall, every J row obeys

`(R_theta x)_e >= -2||x||_max^2`.

Its positive stress sum is zero. The preceding stress bounds therefore
give an upper bound C M||x||_max^2/theta for each row. Apply the inverse:

`||x||_max <= C M^4 ||x||_max^2/theta`.

Thus a distinct feasible cloud is at distance at least
`c theta/M^4`. This is an actual nonlinear isolation radius, not just
full rank or nonzero infinitesimal motion.

## 5. Uniform approximate classification of an arbitrary cloud

For theta<=c M^-40 the effective low-total-slack unit-wall theorem
labels the full cloud by P_(M-1) and bounds its displacement
`||delta||_max<=1000M^4 theta`. This is the previously rederived
Delaunay reconstruction at theta<=1/(10000M^3), not an unspecified
compactness onset. Put d=delta/theta.

Expand every flat nearest-neighbour lower inequality, including all
wall neighbours. Boundary displacement/first-field remainder is at
most C M^3 theta after division by theta; quadratic lower error is
at most C M^8 theta. Write
`epsilon_1=C M^8 theta`.
The individual nested stress has total coefficient 6M and zero work
on the prescribed first corner velocities. Nonnegative approximate
rows imply every strong residual has absolute size at most
`eta=C M^9 theta`.

Project onto L with (8), obtaining d_L with
`||d-d_L||_max<=C M^10 theta`.
Every weak recurrence has lower error at most
`zeta=C M^10 theta`. All subset paths therefore give

`sum_(h in I) t_h >= B_j-rho`, `rho=C M^11 theta`,
`sum t=0`, `B_j=-j(M-j)`.

An explicit correction places t in the exact permutahedron: let
`t_bar=(M-1)*t/(M-1+rho)`.
Since |B_j|>=M-1, multiplying B_j-rho by this factor is at least B_j.
Thus t_bar lies in P, and the initial field bound gives
`||t-t_bar||_2<=C M^15 theta`.

The exact central-chain finite inequality gives chain energy at least
`6 sum a_h^2-C M^5 theta^2`. Replacing d by d_L changes this energy
by at most C M^15 theta. Replacing t by t_bar changes its norm squared
by at most C M^20 theta. Therefore

`0<=sum a_h^2-||t_bar||^2<=C M^20 theta`.

For a convex combination of permutations of a, this deficit is exactly
the average squared distance of those permutations from t_bar. At least
one permutation t* satisfies
`||t_bar-t*||_2<=C M^10 sqrt(theta)`, hence
`||t-t*||_infinity<=C M^15 sqrt(theta)`.

The same prefix/suffix threshold paths, now with lower errors zeta,
bound every s_(r,j) on both sides by its sorting value within
`M*||t-t*||_infinity+M*zeta`. They likewise control alpha_r.
Consequently

`||d-d*||_max<=C M^16 sqrt(theta)`.

The finite sorting packet Q_pi(theta) has remainder at most C M^3 theta^2
from its first field, so

`||old cloud-Q_pi(theta)||_max<=C M^16 theta^(3/2)`.

For theta<=c_*M^-40 choose the universal c_* small enough that this
is strictly below the isolation radius c theta/M^4. The clouds are
therefore exactly equal. Every sorting cloud has an actual center/first-
ring unit triangle. This proves the statement for every M and every
allowed theta, without extracting a subsequence separately for each M.

## 6. Scope audit and next exact obligations

The profile gap used in the positive weights is the arithmetic gap two.
No bound uniform in arbitrarily small gaps of general real profiles is
claimed. Constants in the effective chart, path projection and row norms
are universal; the finite list of smallness inequalities defining c_*
is independent of M. The exponent budget is: first-poly error M^11 theta,
energy deficit M^20 theta, field error M^16 sqrt(theta), isolation
c theta/M^4; hence the final M^-40 window. It also implies every earlier
M^-11, M^-5 and M^-3 smallness requirement after shrinking c_*.

The proof uses all full-chart nearest-neighbour inequalities and exact
wall coordinates. It does not delete old interior isolates or treat their
coordinates as ZR/ZF affine modes. In the z=N branch the triangle is in
the actual old cloud. In z<=N-1 the independently derived strict packet
pays the wall deletion and all source labels with the complete shield/
contact/diameter ledger. These are separate endpoints.

Two next attacks are to improve the polynomial window enough for an
extractable actual wall, and to extend the defect packet to arbitrary
matched/mismatched boundary data supplied by the common Delaunay skeleton.
Exterior cap/core motion and nonbinary face-coupled finite states remain
independent terminal routes. No general container or Target C closure is
claimed at this checkpoint; the continuous goal proceeds.
